1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,083
Let's work through this problem:

2
00:00:02,083 --> 00:00:02,916
Riemann sum.

3
00:00:02,916 --> 00:00:05,000
First we'll see the idea,

4
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,250
then every step,

5
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:08,808
each one checked by a computer.

6
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:12,316
Rectangles under the curve approximate the area;

7
00:00:12,316 --> 00:00:14,032
thinner rectangles do better.

8
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:17,100
Δx = (b − a)/n.

9
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:20,072
Width of each of the 4 rectangles.

10
00:00:20,733 --> 00:00:21,566
Sample points.

11
00:00:21,566 --> 00:00:25,797
Right endpoints: 1/2, 1, 3/2, 2.

12
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,650
f(x₀).

13
00:00:27,650 --> 00:00:30,624
f at x = 1/2.

14
00:00:31,266 --> 00:00:32,516
f(x₁).

15
00:00:32,516 --> 00:00:34,650
f at x = 1.

16
00:00:35,266 --> 00:00:36,516
f(x₂).

17
00:00:36,516 --> 00:00:39,490
f at x = 3/2.

18
00:00:40,133 --> 00:00:41,383
f(x₃).

19
00:00:41,383 --> 00:00:43,517
f at x = 2.

20
00:00:44,133 --> 00:00:47,883
Sum = Δx·(f(x₁) + … ).

21
00:00:47,883 --> 00:00:51,261
Add the heights and multiply by the width.

22
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:55,176
So the answer is 15/4.

23
00:00:55,600 --> 00:01:00,600
Every step you just saw was checked by a computer algebra system,

24
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:03,933
and the final answer was confirmed a second,

25
00:01:03,933 --> 00:01:04,840
independent way.

26
00:01:05,266 --> 00:01:06,516
Find the width,

27
00:01:06,516 --> 00:01:08,183
list the sample points,

28
00:01:08,183 --> 00:01:09,433
evaluate the heights,

29
00:01:09,433 --> 00:01:10,683
add them up,

30
00:01:10,683 --> 00:01:12,826
and multiply by the width.

31
00:01:13,266 --> 00:01:14,933
Now it's your turn.

32
00:01:14,933 --> 00:01:17,850
Pause the video and try this one.

33
